msgid "[x] A role whose upstream path exists but is unreachable here declares the precise blocker instead of being silently absent, and MUST NOT also declare a served surface. Each `blocked` role carries a row naming its reason token and the concrete obstacle, drawn from the per-role guidance the requirement already held. A lint enforced the three halves of that — a blocked role without a row, a token outside the documented vocabulary, and a blocked role shipping an enabled surface — by parsing the audit; it was removed together with the other two document-parsing lints, so the rows are now held by review rather than by a test."
